The vast majority of existing datasets for 3D reconstruction are inadequate due to a limited number of objects or restricted data points. In response, we present a comprehensive database of 3D reconstructions, comprising 2,000 diverse objects gathered from a 3D scanner at 2,400 distinct angles. Each object's reconstruction is accompanied by multiple views capturing various lighting conditions. Our database is designed to facilitate extensive research in the areas of 3D reconstruction and object manipulation. Furthermore, we provide a benchmark for evaluating the performance of 3D reconstruction techniques using our newly established database. Our results demonstrate that the level of detail in 3D reconstructions is directly related to the number of views available, and that the quality of 3D reconstructions can be significantly enhanced by incorporating diverse views. The proposed dataset is publicly available for further research and can be accessed at http://www.vicavision.org/3d-recon. In addition, the accompanying code for processing the dataset is also made available. Users are encouraged to submit their findings for further analysis and to compare their results against those presented in this study. The data is organized according to the following structure: 
